I have two questions.  First, are you using Windows or Linux?

Second, can you send the the code that worked for you?  I keep wondering if I doing something wrong.  Several colleagues, not rNOMADS users, have made suggestions like adding type=”source” but I keep hitting a brick wall.

If you are interested, I‘m trying to correlate low level winds from the Rapid Refresh Forecasts to longitude, latitude, and speed data from a phone ap that tracks hot air balloon flights.  Attached is a flight my wife made in Mesquite Nevada.  By changing altitude, color coded, she tracked back and forth across I-15 six times in an hour.  We joke that the FAA serial number on my father-in-law’s balloon was N-1132R.  And the R stands for ridicules.  We don’t go anywhere...we really don’t accomplish anything.  But it’s kind of a Zen thing.  Controlling the balloon by finding the right wind is such a hoot.

Thanks,
Philip Heinrich
